.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-parhel-add 1  "parhel 0.2.2" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git\-parhel\-add \- Create a copy\-on\-write worktree
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit parhel add\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-new\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-detach\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-dirty\fR] [\fB\-\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-relocate\fR] [\fB\-\-submodules\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDESTINATION\fR> [\fIREFERENCE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a worktree at <destination> by cloning the source worktree with copy\-on\-write, then check out [ref] (default: the source HEAD). Only tracked files that differ between the source HEAD and [ref] are rewritten; everything else, ignored files included, is shared with the source until modified.
.PP
Nothing is created unless every check passes. The worktree is assembled in a hidden .parhel\-staging\-* directory and published with an atomic, exclusive rename: an existing destination is never touched. Failures and Ctrl\-C roll back completely.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<path>\fR [default: .]
Any path inside the source worktree
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<name>\fR
Check out an existing branch
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-branch\fR \fI<name>\fR
Create and check out a new branch
.TP
\fB\-\-detach\fR
Detach HEAD at the target commit
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-dirty\fR
Carry uncommitted changes from the source (staged changes arrive unstaged)
.TP
\fB\-\-fallback\fR
Use a plain `git worktree add` when copy\-on\-write is impossible (no copy\-on\-write on the volume, different volumes)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-relocate\fR
Leave copied files that mention the source\*(Aqs path as they are (by default such paths are rewritten to the new worktree\*(Aqs)
.TP
\fB\-\-submodules\fR \fI<policy>\fR [default: refuse]
Initialized submodules: `refuse`, or `reinit` them with their own git dirs
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
refuse
.IP \(bu 2
reinit
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIDESTINATION\fR>
Where to create the worktree (its parent must exist)
.TP
[\fIREFERENCE\fR]
Commit\-ish to check out (default: the source HEAD)
.SH EXTRA
Exit status: 0 success, 1 error, 2 usage error, 128+N killed by signal N.
Errors are printed as `error[<code>]: <message>` with a stable <code>.
